{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_556245902#0_1166749769","relevance":3,"reason":"This document is dedicated to the 1848 revolutions and directly supports the information need by explaining that the revolutionary movement brought important reforms in the Netherlands and was directed against absolutist Prussia and constitutional monarchies in smaller German states, with social movements in western Germany and Saxony.","learned":"The 1848 revolutions affected the Low Countries with important reforms in the Netherlands, targeted Prussia and smaller German states, and included labor/socialist organizing in western Germany and Saxony."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q14","reason":"The query is yielding high-quality, direct evidence about the 1848 European revolutionary context in both Germany and the Netherlands; continue for more grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q14"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1560430529#0_3281718775","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q14","rank":2,"snippet":"<cover>1848 Revolutions of 1848 European history History at your fingertips \" , \"segment\": \"Revolutions of 1848 | Causes, Summary, & Significance | Britannica Home World History Wars, Battles & Armed Conflicts Revolutions of 1848 European history Print Give Feedback External Websites WRITTEN BY The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica Encyclopaedia Britannica's editors oversee subject areas in which they have extensive knowledge, whether from years of experience gained by working on that content or via study for an advanced degree.... See Article History Revolutions of 1848, series of republican revolts against European monarchies, beginning in Sicily and spreading to France, Germany, Italy, and the Austrian Empire. They all ended in failure and repression and were followed by widespread disillusionment among liberals. Read More on This Topic history of Europe: The Revolutions of 1848 After adopting reforms in the 1830s and the early 1840s, Louis-Philippe of France rejected further change and thereby spurred new liberal... The revolutionary movement began in Italy with a local revolution in Sicily in January 1848, and, after the revolution of February 24 in France, the movement extended throughout the whole of Europe, with the exception of Russia, Spain, and the Scandinavian countries. In the United Kingdom </cover>"}}
